        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Aarsi took shot on cells (1,2),(1,3),(2,1),(2,3),(3,1)(1,2), (1,3), (2,1), (2,3), (3,1)(1,2),(1,3),(2,1),(2,3),(3,1) while Krypto took shot on cells (1,2),(2,3),(3,2),(3,3)(1,2), (2,3), (3,2), (3,3)(1,2),(2,3),(3,2),(3,3).\nConsidering (2,1)(2,1)(2,1) as the bullseye cell, Aarsi's score will be max⁡(∣2−1∣,∣1−2∣)+max⁡(∣2−1∣,∣1−3∣)+max⁡(∣2−2∣,∣1−1∣)+max⁡(∣2−2∣,∣1−3∣)+max⁡(∣2−3∣,∣1−1∣)=6\\max(|2-1|,|1-2|) + \\max(|2-1|,|1-3|) + \\max(|2-2|,|1-1|) + \\max(|2-2|,|1-3|) + \\max(|2-3|,|1-1|) = 6max(∣2−1∣,∣1−2∣)+max(∣2−1∣,∣1−3∣)+max(∣2−2∣,∣1−1∣)+max(∣2−2∣,∣1−3∣)+max(∣2−3∣,∣1−1∣)=6. Similarly, Krypto's score will be 666.\nThus, B(2,1)=∣6−6∣=0B_{(2,1)} = |6-6| = 0B(2,1)​=∣6−6∣=0."
